  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday) \nIssued at 833 PM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nThe main feature of discussion during the long term period will be a\nclosed low system shifting eastward just north of the Great Lakes \nregion, bringing a cold front southeastward into the Tennessee Valley\nby Thursday night. Ahead of and along the frontal boundary, \nincreased chances (30-50%) of showers and thunderstorms are forecast \nThursday afternoon into Friday. While there will likely be a lull in \nstorm activity sometime Friday, this will be short-lived as an upper \nlevel shortwave shifts eastward into the area ahead of an upper level\nridge that is forecast to set up over the southern Plains. Low to \nmedium chances (20-40%) of showers and thunderstorms are forecast to \ncontinue through the weekend. Outside of the mentioned rain chances, \nheat will continue to be a concern. Highs are forecast to remain in \nthe upper 80s to mid 90s with heat indices near 100 degrees. While \nthis is below local Heat Advisory criteria, we encourage everyone to \nremain hydrated and practice heat safety while outdoors.",
